    {
      "id": 234622,
      "name": "der andere Jan",
      "username": "der_andere_Jan",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/der_andere_jan/{size}/1881_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-01-04T20:02:59.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Also, the game tries to balance more than just dice size.</p>\n<p>For example, 'struggling' characters start with significantly smaller dice. But instead, they get access to identity principles, which lend themselves to more versatile and rich roleplaying.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>And of course, the value (or even truth) of the latter is highly subjective, so it seems a good thing that everybody can pick what they deem 'best'.</p>\n<p>But that is a different thing from creating&nbsp;a character in your favourite direction, and then cherrypicking across the (few) fences for even more maximization.</p>\n<p>Of course you can always go 'secret third method', and if that is a workable thing in your group, you win! But in that case it seems moot to discuss chargen&nbsp;rules, because, well, there are none... :)</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:10:45.689Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
